hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28007","Narrated Muhammad ibn Bakr, informed Ibn Jurayj, informed Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, that Abdur-Rahman ibn Tariq ibn Alqamah informed him, from his mother, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whenever he entered a place in the house of Yala, Ubaydullah attributed it, would face the House and supplicate."
"28008","Narrated Abdur-Razzaq, he said: informed Ibn Jurayj, informed Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Tariq ibn Alqamah informed him, from his mother, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whenever he entered a place in the house of Yala, Ubaydullah attributed it, would face the House and supplicate."
"28009","Narrated Ahmad ibn Al-Hajjaj, narrated Abdullah, and Ali ibn Ishaq, informed Abdullah ibn Al-Mubarak, informed Ibn Jurayj, informed Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, that Abdur-Rahman ibn Tariq ibn Alqamah informed him, from his mother, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whenever he entered a place in the house of Yala, Ubaydullah attributed it, would face the House and supplicate. He said: And I and Abdullah ibn Kathir, when we came to that place, would face the House and supplicate."
